Patch 2057: a new fragment program is decompiled where the draw meets it, then its shader compile and pipeline
are built on worker threads (PSO_ASYNC=0 off, PSO_ASYNC_THREADS=N workers, default 4). Draws that need it are
skipped until it is ready.

Each new program cost a 100-400 ms frame on the drawing thread (shader compile ~160 ms plus pipeline ~80 ms), and
J-Stars keeps meeting new ones in fights. The decompile stays on the drawing thread because it reads guest memory
the title may reuse. The batch pre-pass that built a batch's misses in parallel and waited for them is skipped. The
literal-constant scratch buffers of the compile are now per thread.

Tested (US disc, bench.ps1, HITCH=50): frames over 50 ms in Free Battle 2 (before 16-22), demo 4 (one is a 5 s
loading screen); Free Battle 29.90 flips/s, demo 29.05; no crashes; pictures as before
(bench/exp/2026-11-08_1346-async1).

